{"evidence":{"id":"E1","kind":"fact","text":"revenue for fiscal year ending 2013-02-03 = $1,370.4M (XBRL tag SalesRevenueNet)","source":"10-K accession 0001193125-13-118393, filed 2013-03-21"},"origins":{"queries":[{"sql":"SELECT * FROM veritas_pg.facts WHERE cik = 1397187 ORDER BY fy_end, CASE concept WHEN 'revenue' THEN 0 WHEN 'cogs' THEN 1 WHEN 'sga' THEN 2 WHEN 'depreciation' THEN 3 WHEN 'net_income' THEN 4 WHEN 'cfo' THEN 5 WHEN 'receivables' THEN 6 WHEN 'current_assets' THEN 7 WHEN 'ppe' THEN 8 WHEN 'assets' THEN 9 WHEN 'current_liabilities' THEN 10 WHEN 'lt_debt' THEN 11 ELSE 99 END","rows":[{"cik":"1397187","company":"Lululemon","fy_end":"2013-02-03","concept":"revenue","tag":"SalesRevenueNet","value":"1370358000","accn":"0001193125-13-118393","filed":"2013-03-21"}],"mode":"zetaris","label":"executed on Zetaris","table":"facts"}],"rows":[{"cik":"1397187","company":"Lululemon","fy_end":"2013-02-03","concept":"revenue","tag":"SalesRevenueNet","value":"1370358000","accn":"0001193125-13-118393","filed":"2013-03-21"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":1397187,"company":"Lululemon","fy_end":"2014-02-02","activeRevision":"64a4664c5f25","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0001193125-13-118393","filed":"2013-03-21","cik":1397187,"company":"Lululemon","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1397187/000119312513118393/0001193125-13-118393-index.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1397187_2014-02-02","revisionId":"64a4664c5f25","sampleIndex":0,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue growth driven by new store openings, growth of direct-to-consumer segment, and increased comparable store sales (7% total, 9% constant currency).","numbers_show":"Corporate-owned stores segment revenue rose 13% ($138.8M), with new stores contributing $138.0M and comparable store sales adding $19.5M (2% increase). Total revenue grew 16.1% ($1,370.4M to $1,591.2M).","fit":"fits","evidence":["E32","E34","E35","E36","E1","E12"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1397187_2014-02-02","revisionId":"64a4664c5f25","sampleIndex":1,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue growth driven by new stores, comparable store sales increases, and direct-to-consumer growth (E32). Corporate-owned stores up $138.8M, with $138.0M from new stores and $19.5M (2%) / $37.3M (4% constant currency) from comp stores (E34-E36).","numbers_show":"Total revenue rose $220.8M (16.1%) to $1,591.2M (E1, E12, E23). Corporate-owned store segment grew $138.8M (13%) to $1,229M (E34). New store count: 43 in FY2013 (E35). The remainder (~$82M) aligns with 'other net revenue' (wholesale, franchise, showrooms, DTC) cited as a growth driver (E28-E29, E32).","fit":"fits","evidence":["E1","E12","E23","E32","E34","E35","E36"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1397187_2014-02-02","revisionId":"64a4664c5f25","sampleIndex":2,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue growth driven by new store openings, direct-to-consumer growth, and comparable store sales increases (7% total, 9% constant currency). Corporate-owned stores segment rose $138.8M (13%), with new stores contributing $138.0M and comparable stores adding $19.5M.","numbers_show":"Total revenue grew 16.1% ($1,370.4M to $1,591.2M). Corporate-owned stores segment grew 13% ($1,090.2M to $1,229.0M). The implied 'other net revenue' (wholesale, franchise, showrooms) grew ~$82M. Receivables increased $5.5M (87%) but DSO only 2→3 days. CFO flat at $280.1M→$278.3M while net income rose $270.6M→$279.5M.","fit":"fits","evidence":["E1","E12","E23","E32","E34","E35","E36","E7","E18","E6","E17","E5","E16"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}}],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1397187_2014-02-02","revisionId":"64a4664c5f25","sampleIndex":0,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Management cites DTC growth as a revenue driver, but the evidence pack lacks segment data for 'other net revenue' or a separate DTC revenue figure, so the size of this driver cannot be verified.","evidence":["E32","E34","E35","E36","E1","E12"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"Management's stated revenue drivers (new stores, DTC growth, comparable sales) are directly corroborated by segment revenue data showing corporate-owned stores revenue increased $138.8M, with new stores contributing $138.0M and comparable store sales adding $19.5M, together accounting for the segment growth.","evidence":["E34","E35","E36","E1","E12"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1397187_2014-02-02","revisionId":"64a4664c5f25","sampleIndex":1,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Management attributes revenue growth to three drivers: new stores, comparable store sales, and direct-to-consumer/other net revenue growth. The pack provides segment numbers for corporate-owned stores (E34-E36), showing $138.8M growth from that segment, with $138.0M from new stores and $19.5M from comp stores. However, total revenue grew $220.8M (E1, E12), leaving ~$82M unexplained by the corporate-owned store segment. The 'other net revenue' segment (which includes DTC, wholesale, franchise, showrooms) is cited as a growth driver (E28-E29, E32), but its dollar amounts for FY2012 and FY2013 are not in the evidence pack (E33 references a table not provided). Without those reported segment numbers, the size of the third driver cannot be verified.","evidence":["E1","E12","E23","E32","E34","E35","E36"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"Revenue growth is driven by new store openings and comparable store sales gains as reported in segment results. Corporate-owned store revenue rose $138.8M (13%), with $138.0M from 43 new stores opened in FY2013 and $19.5M from a 2% comp store increase. The remaining ~$82M of total revenue growth aligns with the 'other net revenue' segment (wholesale, franchise, showrooms, direct-to-consumer) which management identifies as a growth driver.","evidence":["E1","E12","E23","E32","E34","E35","E36"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.78}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1397187_2014-02-02","revisionId":"64a4664c5f25","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"fits","reason":"Management attributes 16% revenue growth to new stores, direct-to-consumer, and comparable-store gains. The corporate-owned stores segment breakdown shows new stores contributed $138.0M and comparable stores added $19.5M (E34, E35, E36), which together with the $82M rise in 'other net revenue' (implied from total revenue growth of $220.8M per E32 and corporate-owned segment growth of $138.8M per E34) account for the total revenue increase. The named drivers are visible in the segment data and are large enough to explain the pattern.","evidence":["E1","E12","E32","E34","E35","E36","E23"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"Revenue growth is fully explained by new store openings ($138M), comparable store sales growth ($19.5M), and direct-to-consumer expansion, as shown in the corporate-owned stores segment breakdown. The remaining $82M increase in 'other net revenue' (wholesale, franchise, showrooms) is consistent with international showroom openings noted in MD&A.","evidence":["E32","E34","E35","E36","E1","E12","E23"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation fits the numbers","confidence":0.92}}],"audit":[{"seq":1,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1397187_2014-02-02:64a4664c5f25:E1 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":10,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1397187_2014-02-02:64a4664c5f25:E10 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":11,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1397187_2014-02-02:64a4664c5f25:E11 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":12,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1397187_2014-02-02:64a4664c5f25:E12 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":13,"actor"